 "lines": {
  "hook": "You're freezing. Does a drink warm you, or cool you?",
  "b1": "One sip, and a warm glow spreads through you.",
  "b2": "That glow is blood rushing out to your skin.",
  "b3": "So it's card B. It feels warm while you lose heat.",
  "b4": "A lot of alcohol can also weaken shivering, your heater.",
  "b5": "Below about eighty six degrees inside your body, shivering stops.",
  "b6": "One. Put something between you and the frozen ground.",
  "b7": "Two. Cover your head and neck, and get out of the wind.",
  "b8": "Three. Stay dry, and eat something warm and full of calories.",
  "end": "Picked warms you? That warm feeling is your heat leaving."
 },
